  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure settles in for the weekend on the southwestern side of \na mid-level eastern CONUS trough. A dry cold front passage overnight \nFriday night will usher in lower dew points reinforced by dry deep \nlayer northerly flow with local placement between the eastern CONUS \ntrough and central CONUS ridge amid the omega blocking pattern. This \nbrings high probability dry weather with seasonable temperatures \n(highs in 70s, lows in upper 40s/low 50s) through at least next \nTuesday. Chances of rain have gone down even more in the early part \nof next week with shortwaves around the trough displaced east in \nmore recent guidance, and scarce column moisture to work with \n(forecast PWATs near the daily climatological minimum).\n\nTemperature uncertainty increases mid-week with ensembles indecisive \nof ridging or the stagnation of a closed low around the eastern \nseaboard. This may be the difference between remaining seasonable \n(troughing solution) or temperatures trending ~10F above average \nWednesday/Thursday (ridging solution), but most likely dry in any \nscenario.\n\nNext Friday into Saturday, confidence increases in ridging winning \nout, but there is more uncertainty in temperatures affiliated with a \ndigging surface front late-week which will also return the next \nsizable chance of any rain. CIPS also alludes this as the next non-\nzero chance of severe weather.",
